# WN22-AC-000020: Windows Server 2022 must have the number of allowed bad logon attempts configured to three or less.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-ac-000020-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 must have the number of allowed bad logon attempts configured to three or less.`
    description `The account lockout feature, when enabled, prevents brute-force password attacks on the system. The higher this value is, the less effective the account lockout feature will be in protecting the local system. The number of bad logon attempts must be reasonably small to minimize the possibility of a successful password attack while allowing for honest errors made during normal user logon.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,account-policy,security-policy,ksi-iam-jit,ksi-iam-sus`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-JIT,KSI:KSI-IAM-SUS,NIST-800-53:AC-7`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-JIT,KSI-IAM-SUS`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Account Policies >> Account Lockout Policy >> Account lockout threshold to "3" or fewer invalid logon attempts (excluding "0", which is unacceptable).`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_KSI_IAM_JIT `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-JIT by enforcing LockoutBadCount per the STIG (Account lockout threshold must be 1-3 invalid attempts.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_SUS `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-SUS by enforcing LockoutBadCount per the STIG (Account lockout threshold must be 1-3 invalid attempts.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_AC_7 `Windows Server implements AC-7 by enforcing LockoutBadCount per the STIG (Account lockout threshold must be 1-3 invalid attempts.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `LockoutBadCount`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int >= 1
        value_int int <= 3
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
